1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
For five seconds gravity lets go

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,370
of the garden, and one small

3
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:04,850
hop puts Gus higher than his

4
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:05,310
roof.

5
00:00:05,354 --> 00:00:06,754
It's ten on a Sunday morning

6
00:00:06,954 --> 00:00:08,514
and Gus is flipping a pancake

7
00:00:08,524 --> 00:00:09,284
in his garden.

8
00:00:09,328 --> 00:00:10,778
Then gravity switches off.

9
00:00:11,048 --> 00:00:12,538
The pancake leaves the pan at

10
00:00:12,548 --> 00:00:13,698
eight feet a second and just

11
00:00:13,708 --> 00:00:14,438
keeps going.

12
00:00:14,482 --> 00:00:15,942
His neighbor yells that the Earth

13
00:00:15,952 --> 00:00:17,542
spins at eight hundred miles an

14
00:00:17,552 --> 00:00:19,052
hour, so they'll be flung into

15
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:19,672
space.

16
00:00:19,726 --> 00:00:20,856
His wife sits still.

17
00:00:21,116 --> 00:00:22,316
In five seconds the spinning

18
00:00:22,326 --> 00:00:23,906
ground sinks ten inches under her

19
00:00:23,916 --> 00:00:24,456
chair.

20
00:00:24,646 --> 00:00:25,226
That's all.

21
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:26,280
Don't move, she says.

22
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:27,920
But Gus wants his pancake, so

23
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:28,570
he hops.

24
00:00:28,624 --> 00:00:29,714
That hop is good for one

25
00:00:29,724 --> 00:00:30,114
foot.

26
00:00:30,374 --> 00:00:31,784
So why is he sailing past

27
00:00:31,794 --> 00:00:32,474
his chimney?

28
00:00:32,518 --> 00:00:33,978
You see, gravity is a brake.

29
00:00:34,258 --> 00:00:35,378
Roll a ball up a hill

30
00:00:35,388 --> 00:00:36,768
and the hill eats its speed.

31
00:00:36,822 --> 00:00:37,962
Take the hill away and the

32
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:39,842
ball rolls on across the floor,

33
00:00:40,042 --> 00:00:41,352
as fast as it started.

34
00:00:41,406 --> 00:00:42,836
Gus leaves the lawn at eight

35
00:00:42,846 --> 00:00:44,016
feet a second and keeps it

36
00:00:44,026 --> 00:00:44,436
all.

37
00:00:44,716 --> 00:00:46,496
Four seconds later he's thirty two

38
00:00:46,506 --> 00:00:46,966
feet up.

39
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,600
The pancake left a second sooner

40
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:50,130
at the same speed, so it

41
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:51,790
stays eight feet out of reach.

42
00:00:51,844 --> 00:00:53,154
Then gravity comes back.

43
00:00:53,394 --> 00:00:54,914
Gus coasts up one more foot

44
00:00:54,924 --> 00:00:55,844
and starts down.

45
00:00:55,898 --> 00:00:57,278
Luckily, that's the height of an

46
00:00:57,288 --> 00:00:58,998
Olympic diving tower, and the

47
00:00:59,008 --> 00:01:00,118
neighbor has a pool.

48
00:01:00,162 --> 00:01:02,042
Unluckily, Gus is no diver.

49
00:01:02,292 --> 00:01:03,542
He hits the water at thirty

50
00:01:03,552 --> 00:01:04,462
miles an hour.

51
00:01:04,506 --> 00:01:05,896
A moment later the pancake comes

52
00:01:05,906 --> 00:01:08,006
down too, right on Gus.
